    "noble_behavior": "__smmu_client_set_hwgrp_default() turns off the final group through its ASID register alone. SMMU_ASID_ENABLE is bit31; ASID indices use the remaining defined fields.",
    "upstream_explanation": "https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/10/16/631",
    "upstream_scope": "NVIDIA-authored Tegra210 display handover proposal explicitly describes bypass with ASID_ENABLE clear while per-client enables remain set. Used as hardware-contract corroboration, not as an installed Linux patch.",
