    "global_config": "The cause of the native 0xffffffff CONFIG readback remains unresolved. No value or permission result is substituted; the resource snapshot still reports REGS_INVALID and leaves BOOT_REGS_VALID clear.",
    "no_smmu_writes": true
  },
  "changes": [
    "Live H.264 routing requires clear, non-all-ones HC and NVDEC ASID_ENABLE readbacks; per-client enable words no longer create a false rejection.",
    "An enabled group remains rejected even when per-client enables are clear. NVJPG remains a power dependency and is not a DMA client of this H.264 backend.",
    "The resource snapshot preserves raw enable words and derives its three-group route flag from group ASID_ENABLE. Invalid ASID or MC flush readbacks still reject client validity.",
    "Private ABI layouts and versions remain unchanged; comments define the existing flag scope. Adapter-start snapshots remain separate from live ownership and completion."
  ],
